INT. CORPORATE WELLNESS NAP POD ROOM - DAY

Six sleep pods. One occupied. Whale sounds on a loop.

PRIYA DESHMUKH-LOWE, 30s, lanyard, laptop balanced on her knees inside the pod. Typing in the dark.

The hatch hisses open. WALTER "WALLY" PRZYBYSZ, 50s, regional VP, leans in with a clipboard.

WALLY
Priya. Nap quota's twenty minutes.

PRIYA
This is a nap.

WALLY
You're answering email.

PRIYA
Napping with intent.

Wally ticks a box. Writes. Frowns.

Behind him, the door swings. DR. SUNNIVA ABARA, 40s, Chief Wellbeing Officer, crisp blazer, tablet like a shield.

SUNNIVA
Walter. Is she charging overage?

WALLY
She's... overachieving.

SUNNIVA
(to Priya)
I need you rested for the layoff announcement.

Priya's typing stops. Wally's pen stops. The whales go on.

PRIYA
When?

SUNNIVA
After your nap.

Priya closes the laptop. Smiles. Lies back, hands folded like a corpse.

WALLY
(whisper to Sunniva)
She knows.

SUNNIVA
She knows nothing.

Priya snores. Loudly. Fakely.

Wally sweats. Sunniva checks her watch. The whales sing.
